WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
SPEAKER 1: MacArthur
criticized Truman publicly,

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.080
said there is no
substitute for victory.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.984
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.720
There wasn't much time after the
victory over Germany and Japan

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.590
for popping champagne
corks and celebrating.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.450
Just as the 50 nations that had
joined in defeating the Axis

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.009
powers were drafting a
charter for the United Nations

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:35.010
in San Francisco,
victorious alliance

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.410
between the United States
and the Soviet Union

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.480
was falling apart.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.000
War alliance between
the United States

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.200
and Britain and the Soviet
Union was tactical exclusively.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.890
There was no other ideological
or sentimental attachment

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.280
between the nations.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:58.450
And as the war appeared to be
won in Europe, spring of 1945,

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:03.150
the Red Army began occupying
more and more portions

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:08.100
of Eastern Europe with the
clear intention of establishing

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.450
a Soviet Empire.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.940
This is exactly what
Churchill was worried about.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.300
In March of 1946,
Winston Churchill

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.010
gave a speech in America in
which he uttered a phrase that

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.900
would live on for a long time.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.420
He said that "from
Stettin in the Baltic

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.040
to Trieste in the Adriatic,
an Iron Curtain has descended

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.820
across the continent."

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:36.150
So what to do about this
expansionist tendency,

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.640
short of fighting a war?

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.090
Well, what Truman arrived
at was a conclusion heavily

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.270
influenced by the
writings of George Kennan,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.660
an American diplomat
in Russia, who

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.300
believed that Soviet
expansionism was actually

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.040
a result of the insecure,
unstable nature of the regime

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.450
itself, and that the
process of expansion

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.990
was actually a way of
holding that regime together.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.940
And that if expansion was
prevented, if it was contained,

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.280
then the regime, in
due course, would

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.130
turn in on itself and collapse.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.380
This doctrine came to
be known as containment,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.360
because it was a way of fighting
the Soviet regime by containing

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.760
it rather than by defeating it.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.480
At any rate, a
sustained confrontation

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.360
between the two
remaining superpowers

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.470
in the world that would come
to be called the Cold War.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.720
The Cold War turned hot in
1950 on the Korean Peninsula,

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.970
which had been
divided since the end

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.150
of the war between
communist forces

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.670
in the north that were
aligned with the Soviet Union

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.560
and Democratic
forces in the South

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.330
that were aligned with
the United States.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:55.620
This led to an invasion
on June 25, 1950

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.230
of some 80,000 North
Korean troops that

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:03.690
swept into the South,
very nearly conquering it.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:08.850
And Truman invoked
the United Nations.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.240
And the American response was
funneled through the United

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.160
Nations, as it was
called a police

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.220
action rather than a war.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.020
There was no declaration of war.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.670
The war went very badly until
General Douglas MacArthur

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:28.410
got involved, performed a
brilliant amphibious invasion

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.980
at Inchon, which cut off
the North Korean troops

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.030
and led him quickly to
be able to around them

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.340
up, defeat them,
and then head north.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.970
And they kept going north
and finally approached

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.410
the Chinese border.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.800
And at that point, a quarter
of a million Chinese troops

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:53.820
swept in on MacArthur and drove
him back into South Korea,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.160
with the battle line
finally stabilizing

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.730
around the 38th parallel.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.970
At this point,
MacArthur and Truman

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:08.570
got deadlocked in a conflict,
because MacArthur thought

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.760
the time was right,
the justification

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.210
was there for what he
called a whole new war--

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.300
a war against China,
against communist China,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.899
that would succeed
in overthrowing

00:04:21.899 --> 00:04:27.600
this unfriendly, hostile,
noxious communist regime that

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:33.570
had just taken
power and thus avert

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:40.110
the prospect of a Sino-Soviet
Chinese and Soviet alliance

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.570
that could come to
dominate the world.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.580
The time was right
to take that on.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.620
Truman, on the
other hand, thought

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.050
this was absolutely
the wrong thing--

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.870
that it would be, he
called it, a booby trap

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:58.740
to go into a war in China
and rejected the idea.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.370
MacArthur criticized
Truman publicly.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.430
In an official letter to
the House Minority Leader,

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.770
said there is no
substitute for victory--

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:12.030
in other words, a rejection
of the containment doctrine.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.720
There is no
prettifying the fact,

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.160
though, that the Korean War
was, at best, a stalemate.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.640
It remains a people divided.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.940
To this day, there is no
settlement of the war.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.390
The war is simply suspended.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.810
So in some ways,
it illustrates some

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.160
of the unsatisfactory aspects
of the containment doctrine.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.810
And that situation is
yet to be resolved.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.260
SPEAKER 2: Thank
you for watching.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.230
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlights series

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.140
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.310
online courses.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:51.470
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

